# Keel's test fixtures are byte-exact inputs: the graph scanners tokenize them, the diff parser
# matches hunk bodies against them line for line, and several tests assert on exact strings. A
# CRLF working tree would change those bytes, so pin the checkout to LF on every platform
# regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf. (The Windows CI leg turns autocrlf off too.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: the tree-sitter grammars and the phase-0 git bundle.
*.wasm binary
*.bundle binary
